{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794410641,"nonce":"uFJSQcN6acR/pGrfzaxzouJH0b0=","title":"Collection for native memory: what hxn does and what is still open","message":"A collector runs when the memory it manages has grown. An object that owns a\nhandle is a few words of that whatever the value behind it holds, so a program\ncan drop a great deal of native memory and never be due a collection. Before\nthis hxn offered `close()` and finalizers and nothing that caused a collection.\n\n\n- `hxn.Gc.collect()`: `hl.Gc.major()` on HashLink and Ash, `cpp.vm.Gc.run(true)`\n  on hxcpp, and nothing under Emscripten, where it returns false.\n- `hxn::Weight` (in `hxn-abi`, `memory.rs`): kept in a value, counted into a\n  per-library total while the value lives. `set` follows a size that changes;\n  `Clone` counts as much again.\n- `hxn::collect_soon()`: a flag, taken by the next check.\n- Every adapter exports `\u003clibrary\u003e_memory_held` and `\u003clibrary\u003e_memory_wanted`.\n- `hxn.Gc.Meter`, one per library (`Hxn\u003cLibrary\u003eMemory.meter` in generated\n  bindings). `check()` collects when the library asked, or when the total is\n  over `max(hxn.Gc.budget, 2 x what was left after the last collection run\n  from here)`. The budget defaults to 64 MiB.\n- An interface marked `#[hxn::interface(weighed)]` checks when one of its\n  objects is made: in the constructor and in `adopt` on HashLink, in `own` on\n  hxcpp. `Inbox.sync` checks every meter, and `Loop.sync` does when no library\n  has an inbox.\n\n\nhxcpp has `hx::GCChangeManagedMemory(delta, why)` for memory it does not\nmanage, and the first plan was to feed it. Reading hxcpp 4.3.2\n(`src/hx/gc/Immix.cpp`):\n\n- `onMemoryChange` begins `if (hx::gPauseForCollect) __hxcpp_gc_safe_point();`.\n  During a collection that flag is set, and `PauseForCollect` then stops with\n  \"Bad Allocation while collecting - from finalizer?\". So a finalizer cannot\n  report what it released.\n- `Collect` runs finalizers and afterwards sets\n  `mLargeAllocForceRefresh = mLargeAllocated + mLargeAllocSpace`. With releases\n  reported only after the collection, `mLargeAllocated` still counts what the\n  collection just freed, so the next threshold sits a whole batch higher. With\n  nothing else collecting in between, the garbage allowed to pile up grows by\n  `mLargeAllocSpace` (40 MiB to begin with) every cycle: 40, 80, 120, ...\n\nSo the meter reads the total itself and calls `cpp.vm.Gc.run(true)`, the same\npolicy as on HashLink. hxcpp is not told about the memory at all.\n\n\n- Checking on every object a binding makes, with no mark. No configuration,\n  but two native calls per object for libraries whose values are small. The\n  mark keeps it to interfaces whose author says they are heavy.\n- A fixed weight on the attribute (`weight = N`). Cannot follow a value that\n  grows, and the release still has to be counted natively because a HashLink\n  finalizer cannot run Haxe. `Weight::new(N)` in the constructor covers it.\n- Reading the total as an atomic cell by address, to avoid the call. The cell\n  is 32 bits and the total is not.\n- One total for the process. `hxn-abi` is linked into each library, so the\n  total is per library and so is the budget.\n\n\n`tests/counter/haxe/Generated.hx`, 400 blobs of 1 MiB dropped without `close`,\nbudget 8 MiB: at most 8 MiB held at any check, on Ash (hybrid, jit, interp),\nstock HashLink 1.15 on the NUC and hxcpp 4.3.2. A request from the library\ncollects four blobs that are under the budget.\n\n\n- Generated bindings do not run on wasm or under Emscripten yet (see the\n  generator issue), so the meter is unexercised there. Only `hxn.Gc.collect()`\n  is, through the hand-written fixture.\n- Under Emscripten nothing can force a collection, so a meter only counts.\n  Whether `GCChangeManagedMemory` is usable there, where hxcpp's own trigger\n  does work, has not been tried.\n- A value that grows (`Weight::set`) is counted, but growing checks nothing:\n  only making an object and a delivery do.\n- A check that finds another thread checking returns at once. Fine for a\n  meter; not a guarantee that a collection ran before the caller continues.\n- hxcpp built with its generational collector: `run(true)` is a major\n  collection, which is what is wanted, but this was not run in that mode.\n- The hand-written fixture bindings have no meter.\n- No Haxe-side way for an app to give its own weight to a Haxe object.","files":null}]}